      "writtenOn": "2025-01-23T15:26:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This script will be called via the IDE hook (VsCode, vim, etc) and won\u0027t be lunched. You could lunch and then launch vscode-server (the remote endpoint for VsCode) but then if you wanted to switch lunch targets you would have to close out of the IDE and kill vscode-server. This allows us to read in the env variables of the currently set lunch target. Since each invocation of the script will read from this file, any lunch updates will be handled on the next invocation of `check_rust`.\n\nNot sure what your workflow is but generally mine is the following\n1. Launch VsCode on connected to a remote target\n2. Open a terminal in VsCode\n3. lunch target\n3. Start hacking on a file\n4. Build module via `m module_name`\n5. Discover issues, goto step 3\n\nSometimes I will switch lunch targets mid development if I am testing a change out on multiple devices. I do not close my IDE when I switch lunch targets.",
      "parentUuid": "0aeb54bd_2e8b3fdc",
      "revId": "c0b190a88cfa679e1ad17d0b0fc7134e27135f17",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
